---
// a script is a line. an agent is a loop. a small dot rides the loop so the eye follows it.
---

<figure>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 300" role="img" aria-label="Left: a script goes question, SQL, number in a straight line. Right: an agent goes look, act, check, and on failure learns and acts again, up to three tries, then answers or stops.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="arrowhead" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 Z" fill="#898781"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="90" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="label">a script</text>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(30 44)"><rect width="120" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="60" y="21" text-anchor="middle">question</text></g>
    <path class="arrow" d="M90 76 V100"></path>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(30 104)"><rect width="120" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="60" y="21" text-anchor="middle">SQL</text></g>
    <path class="arrow" d="M90 136 V160"></path>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(30 164)"><rect width="120" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="60" y="21" text-anchor="middle">number</text></g>
    <text x="90" y="226" text-anchor="middle" class="note">right or wrong,</text>
    <text x="90" y="242" text-anchor="middle" class="note">it prints</text>

    <line x1="210" x2="210" y1="30" y2="280" class="divider"></line>

    <text x="410" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="label">an agent</text>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(300 44)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">look</text></g>
    <path class="arrow" d="M355 76 V104"></path>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(300 108)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">act</text></g>
    <path class="arrow" d="M355 140 V168"></path>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(300 172)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">check</text></g>

    <path class="arrow" d="M410 188 H478"></path>
    <text x="444" y="182" text-anchor="middle" class="note">pass</text>
    <g class="box answer" transform="translate(482 172)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">answer</text></g>

    <path class="arrow" d="M355 204 V232"></path>
    <text x="372" y="222" class="note">fail</text>
    <g class="box" transform="translate(300 236)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">learn</text></g>

    <path class="arrow" d="M300 252 H270 V124 H296"></path>
    <text x="262" y="192" text-anchor="end" class="note">again,</text>
    <text x="262" y="206" text-anchor="end" class="note">3 tries</text>

    <path class="arrow" d="M410 252 H478"></path>
    <text x="444" y="246" text-anchor="middle" class="note">after 3</text>
    <g class="box stop" transform="translate(482 236)"><rect width="110" height="32" rx="6"></rect><text x="55" y="21" text-anchor="middle">stop, say why</text></g>

    <circle class="dot" r="4"></circle>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>A script is a line. An agent is a loop with a check in it and a limit on how many times it goes around.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .label {
    font-size: 12px;
    fill: #898781;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .box rect {
    fill: #fff;
    stroke: #c3c2b7;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .box text {
    font-size: 13px;
    fill: #212529;
  }

  .box.answer rect {
    stroke: #212529;
  }

  .box.stop rect {
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .arrow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: #898781;
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    marker-end: url(#arrowhead);
  }

  .divider {
    stroke: #e1e0d9;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .note {
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: #898781;
  }

  /* the dot rides the loop: act -> check -> learn -> back to act */
  .dot {
    fill: #2a78d6;
    offset-path: path("M355 140 V252 H270 V124 H355 Z");
    animation: ride 7s linear infinite;
  }

  @keyframes ride {
    to {
      offset-distance: 100%;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .dot {
      animation: none;
      offset-distance: 0%;
    }
  }
</style>
